# Kernel config fragment — Libre Computer Le/La Frite (Amlogic GXL) LIGHT desktop.
#
# Applied on top of the chosen base defconfig by build-frite-stage4.sh using
# scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh, which correctly handles Kconfig dependency
# resolution. Two jobs:
#   1) Keep the SAME hardening posture as the rest of the fleet (SELinux LSM,
#      lockdown-friendly, audit) — the SELinux guard in the builder enforces it.
#   2) Enable the Amlogic Meson platform + a lean DRM/KMS + input + USB so the
#      lean desktop actually displays and takes a keyboard/mouse on the SBC.
#
# We build from a generic arm64 defconfig (the builder passes -d defconfig), which
# already enables the broad ARCH_MESON platform; this fragment pins the bits the
# light desktop + the hardened posture specifically need.
#
# Format: standard .config fragment (CONFIG_FOO=y / # CONFIG_FOO is not set /
# CONFIG_FOO="string") — consumed by merge_config.sh, NOT by scripts/config.

# ── Amlogic Meson GXL platform (S805X / S905X) ─────────────────────
CONFIG_ARCH_MESON=y
CONFIG_MESON_GXL_PHY=y
CONFIG_MESON_SARADC=y
CONFIG_MESON_GX_SOCINFO=y
# Onboard 100M Ethernet (dwmac-meson)
CONFIG_STMMAC_ETH=y
CONFIG_DWMAC_MESON=y
# eMMC / SD (MMC host on the GXL)
CONFIG_MMC=y
CONFIG_MMC_MESON_GX=y
# SPI NOR (La Frite boots u-boot from SPI; useful to read/identify it from Linux)
CONFIG_SPI=y
CONFIG_SPI_MESON_SPIFC=y
CONFIG_MTD=y
CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR=y

# ── USB (La Frite has NO SD slot — USB is the LIVE root path) ──────
CONFIG_USB=y
CONFIG_USB_DWC2=y
CONFIG_USB_DWC3=y
CONFIG_USB_DWC3_MESON_G12A=y
CONFIG_USB_STORAGE=y
CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_HID=y
CONFIG_HID_GENERIC=y

# ── Display / DRM (meson KMS + Mali-450 'lima') ────────────────────
CONFIG_DRM=y
CONFIG_DRM_MESON=y
CONFIG_DRM_MESON_DW_HDMI=y
CONFIG_DRM_LIMA=y
CONFIG_FB=y
CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=y

# ── Input ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CONFIG_INPUT_EVDEV=y
CONFIG_INPUT_KEYBOARD=y
CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSE=y

# ── Virtual display under the containerised QEMU runner (SPICE, guest resize) ──
# launch-arm.sh boots this Image on `-M virt` (--virt-dtb: QEMU's own DTB, since
# the board DTB cannot describe virt's PCIe/virtio) and, in display mode, attaches
# `-device virtio-gpu-pci,edid=on` + SPICE + a vdagent channel + usb-tablet/usb-kbd
# behind `-device qemu-xhci`. The generic arm64 defconfig this fragment merges
# onto carries VIRTIO_PCI/VIRTIO_MMIO/VIRTIO_CONSOLE and INPUT_MISC but NEITHER
# virtio-gpu NOR virtio-input, so without these three lines the emulated desktop
# is serial-only. The deps are restated so the fragment is self-sufficient:
# DRM_VIRTIO_GPU depends on DRM (above) + VIRTIO_MENU; VIRTIO_INPUT on VIRTIO;
# INPUT_UINPUT on INPUT_MISC (olddefconfig drops a leaf whose menu is off, with
# no message). Inert on the real board: nothing binds without a virtio bus.
CONFIG_VIRTIO=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_MENU=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_PCI=y
CONFIG_DRM_VIRTIO_GPU=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_INPUT=y
CONFIG_INPUT_MISC=y
CONFIG_INPUT_UINPUT=y
# ── QEMU emulation of the board (tests/qemu; INERT on the SBC) ─────
# The S805X has no PCI bus and no virtio transport, so nothing below ever probes
# on the board: the cost is Image bytes, nothing else. In `qemu-system-aarch64
# -M virt` they are what makes the Frite INSTALLER provable end to end (boot the
# medium, install to an emulated eMMC, boot the eMMC, screendump the greeter):
#   * MMC_SDHCI_PCI  — QEMU's `emmc` device (boot0/boot1 partitions, device/type
#     = MMC under /sys/block, i.e. exactly how La Frite's eMMC appears) attaches
#     through `sdhci-pci`. =y, NOT =m: the installed plaintext root boots with NO
#     initramfs (root=PARTUUID on the eMMC), so a module could never be loaded
#     in time and the installed system would panic looking for its root.
#   * DRM_VIRTIO_GPU — a KMS head for `-device virtio-gpu-pci` so lightdm/Xorg
#     draw and a QMP screendump shows the greeter (DRM_VIRTIO_GPU_KMS is
#     `default y` on it; DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION above gives the console too).
#   * VIRTIO_INPUT   — virtio keyboard/tablet so the login can be typed.
#   * VIRTIO_PCI     — the transport both virtio devices sit on.
#   * PCI, MMC_SDHCI — what MMC_SDHCI_PCI / VIRTIO_PCI / USB_XHCI_PCI `depends on`.
#   * PCI_HOST_GENERIC — the ECAM host controller `-M virt` presents its PCIe bus
#     through. Without it there is NO bus for the three *_PCI drivers to probe,
#     and nothing else in the fragment notices (it has a prompt, so a trimming
#     `# CONFIG_PCI_HOST_GENERIC is not set` would be honoured without a word).
#     The arm64 defconfig sets all of these; they are pinned here so a
#     --defconfig override cannot prune the block above with no message
#     (olddefconfig drops a symbol whose dependency is off, silently).
# USB_XHCI_PCI (qemu-xhci + usb-storage = the installer medium as /dev/sda, like
# the real USB stick) is a promptless `default y` DERIVED from PCI + USB_PCI +
# USB_XHCI_HCD (set above); it cannot be requested here, so
# tests/scripts/test-frite-kernel-emulation-symbols.sh guards its inputs instead
# (no `# CONFIG_PCI / USB_PCI / USB_XHCI_HCD is not set` may ever enter this
# fragment) and, given a kernel tree, resolves the whole fragment to prove it.
CONFIG_PCI=y
CONFIG_PCI_HOST_GENERIC=y
CONFIG_MMC_SDHCI=y
CONFIG_MMC_SDHCI_PCI=y
# DRM_VIRTIO_GPU, VIRTIO_INPUT and VIRTIO_PCI are requested ONCE, in the
# virtual-display block above (each must have exactly one assignment:
# tests/scripts/test-frite-kernel-emulation-symbols.sh).

# ── Audio (lean — HDMI/I2S via the meson card; ALSA only) ──────────
CONFIG_SOUND=y
CONFIG_SND=y
CONFIG_SND_SOC=y
CONFIG_SND_MESON_GX_SOUND_CARD=y

# ── zram swap (the 512 MB SKU leans on this) ──────────────────────
CONFIG_ZRAM=y
CONFIG_ZSMALLOC=y
CONFIG_SWAP=y

# ── LUKS2 root (dm-crypt) — --encrypt-root standalone builds ──────
# CONFIG_MD gates the whole drivers/md/Kconfig subtree (BLK_DEV_DM/DM_CRYPT both
# `depends on` it, directly or transitively) — without it, `make olddefconfig`
# silently drops BLK_DEV_DM/DM_CRYPT regardless of what's requested below.
# CONFIG_BLK_DEV_DM is enabled further BELOW in this same file (the LIVE overlay
# path) — merge_config.sh merges the whole fragment as a flat set before a single
# olddefconfig resolves the dependency graph, so file order doesn't matter, but
# CONFIG_MD does still need to be requested somewhere in the merged set.
# This adds the actual crypt target + cipher/hash primitives so a LUKS2 root
# unlocks via the disk-boot dracut initramfs (build-frite-stage4.sh's
# --encrypt-root path). CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK is the ARMv8 Crypto Extensions
# accelerator — the crypto API auto-selects it at runtime only if the specific
# board's Cortex-A53 actually implements the optional AES extension; harmless
# no-op otherwise. Mirrors specs-rpi5/kernel/hardened-k8s.config.
CONFIG_MD=y
CONFIG_DM_CRYPT=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_XTS=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA512=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_HASH=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER=y
# Disable hibernation — resume-from-disk bypasses LUKS2 disk encryption.
# Mirrors specs-x86/kernel/hardened-k8s.config and specs-rpi5/kernel/hardened-k8s.config.
# CONFIG_HIBERNATION is not set

# ── Hardening posture (MUST match the fleet; guarded by the builder) ─
# SECURITY_NETWORK must come before SECURITY_SELINUX — selinux depends on it.
CONFIG_SECURITY=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_NETWORK=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_BOOTPARAM=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_YAMA=y
# Kernel lockdown (cmdline: lockdown=integrity). Mirrors specs-x86 + specs-rpi5; the
# 8 ARM boards used to ship neither the symbol nor the cmdline token. It SELECTS
# CONFIG_MODULE_SIG (Kconfig: `select MODULE_SIG if MODULES`), so every module this
# build installs is signed with the kernel's auto-generated key and an UNSIGNED or
# out-of-tree .ko is refused at runtime once lockdown=integrity is on. _EARLY makes
# lockdown run before every other LSM so the boot parameters are covered too.
CONFIG_SECURITY_LOCKDOWN_LSM=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_LOCKDOWN_LSM_EARLY=y
CONFIG_AUDIT=y
CONFIG_AUDITSYSCALL=y
CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y
# `bpf` is deliberately NOT in this list. The kernel silently DROPS an LSM name
# whose module is absent — it prints a SHORTER "LSM: initializing lsm=..." and
# boots on — and CONFIG_BPF_LSM has never been set in ANY board fragment in this
# repo, nor are its Kconfig deps (BPF_JIT, BPF_EVENTS) enabled here. So the name
# only ever advertised a posture the running kernel did not have. yama IS real on
# this board (CONFIG_SECURITY_YAMA=y above). Re-add `bpf` only together with
# CONFIG_BPF_LSM + its deps AND a verified board build; the builder guard now
# derives the required CONFIG_* set from this very string and will fail without it.
# lockdown is listed FIRST so it activates before any other LSM (as on x86/rpi5).
CONFIG_LSM="lockdown,yama,selinux"
# ASLR / stack / slab hardening
CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_BASE=y
CONFIG_STACKPROTECTOR_STRONG=y
CONFIG_SLAB_FREELIST_HARDENED=y
CONFIG_SLAB_FREELIST_RANDOM=y
CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY=y
CONFIG_FORTIFY_SOURCE=y

# ── tun + iptables (tailscale needs /dev/net/tun + nf) ─────────────
CONFIG_TUN=y
CONFIG_NETFILTER=y
CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK=y
CONFIG_IP_NF_IPTABLES=y
CONFIG_NETFILTER_XTABLES=y

# ── Squashfs + overlay + loop (the LIVE flavor boots a squashfs) ──
# The LIVE flavor boots a dracut dmsquash-live initramfs that mounts
# LiveOS/squashfs.img read-only (loop + squashfs) and stacks a writable overlay
# = the ephemeral root. We use the overlayfs overlay (rd.live.overlay.overlayfs=1
# on the cmdline), but device-mapper + dm-snapshot are also enabled so dracut's
# default DM overlay path works too. tmpfs/devtmpfs are required for the initramfs
# (it mounts /dev via devtmpfs and the writable overlay on tmpfs).
CONFIG_SQUASHFS=y
CONFIG_SQUASHFS_XZ=y
CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y
CONFIG_ISO9660_FS=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_DM=y
CONFIG_DM_SNAPSHOT=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM=y
CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
CONFIG_TMPFS=y
CONFIG_TMPFS_POSIX_ACL=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y
